 "source_passage": "Business-management / accounting / payroll SaaS for SMEs and mid-market — high data sensitivity (custodian of payroll, TFNs, bank details for many client businesses). Confirmed high-severity 2019 payroll incident: an AccountRight Live glitch sent/exposed payment summaries and payslips to wrong recipients across employers, exposing salaries, names, addresses, TFNs and bank details; reported to OAIC and ATO. Incident is dated (2019) and was a glitch rather than an external breach, hence Medium rather than High. KKR-owned (private), large user base (~1.2M), and a fresh April 2026 Microsoft AI partnership expanding its tech footprint. 2019 payroll/payslip data exposure (AccountRight Live glitch): salaries, names, addresses, TFNs, bank details sent to wrong people; OAIC + ATO notified (Notifiable Data Breach) 2019 incident corroborated by independent media UpGuard 'A' rating (825/950) but flags infostealer malware detected on associated systems plus CSP/DNSSEC/HSTS hygiene gaps (low-confidence automated signal) Parent/owner: KKR (acquired ~A$2bn in 2019, delisted from ASX); former PE owners Bain Capital (2011-19), Archer Capital (2009-11) Strategic tech partner: Microsoft (five-year AI partnership signed Apr 2026; 'Powered by Microsoft') Subsidiaries/brands: Tall Emu (CRM), Flare HR (HR/payroll fintech), Nimbus Portal Solutions (doc mgmt), GreatSoft (practice mgmt) Competitors: Xero (market leader ~60%), Intuit QuickBooks, Reckon Clarifying finding: the 'Endeavour' MYOB implementation partner is a NZ ERP consultancy, NOT ASX-listed Endeavour Group (name collision)",
